  "id": "cube-model",
  "term": "cube model",
  "definition": "In this source, the cube model refers to P-Cube, a multi-step prediction approach designed to handle differences within a mixed population by first identifying distinct subgroups and then estimating outcomes within each subgroup. It is used to find subgroup-specific risk factors and give more personalized predictions than a single model applied to everyone together.",
